activation-mlp-act.patch  (notes/research-activations.md; side quests SQ160-SQ162; claims C200-C209)

Opt-in MLP activation: ModelConfig.mlp_act (default "swiglu" = bit-identical to today, same parameter names so existing
checkpoints load). Adds three candidates, all parameter- and FLOP-matched to the SwiGLU at the same mlp_hidden:
  relu2            ungated ReLU^2 (BitNet b1.58 2B4T / Primer / Nemotron-4), one up-projection of width 1.5*mlp_hidden
  xielu            ungated xIELU (arXiv 2411.13010), width 1.5*mlp_hidden, +2 scalars per MLP (alpha_p, alpha_n)
  swiglu_relu2mix  SwiGLU whose gate activation is a learnable per-channel blend of SiLU and ReLU^2 (+h params) [speculation]
Not included (follow-ups): gogeta/hf.py GogetaConfig needs the mlp_act field for HF export. (train.py already puts every
p.dim() < 2 parameter, i.e. the 0-d xIELU alphas and the 1-d mix vector, in the no-decay group: nothing to change there.)
